  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sewage Rehabilitation to increase access to irrigation water from Duma Canal -SH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam team will do rehabilitation of sanitary Sewage System in the agriculture lands to increase the access to cultivated land and reduce the affect of sewage water on the irrigation water in Rural Damascus  - Douma By improving the sewage infrastructure and reducing the contamination of irrigation water, the project ensures safer and more reliable access to clean water for agricultural use. This directly supports farmers (both women and men) in maintaining and improving crop production, which strengthens local food availability and income generation. Cleaner irrigation water also protects soil fertility and prevents crop damage, helping farmers sustain their livelihoods over time despite recurrent shocks such as droughts or economic instability. In addition, the intervention enhances community health and living conditions by minimizing the risks of waterborne diseases, thereby improving overall well -being. Through these combined effects, the project contributes to more resilient communities with better access to food, safer environments, and sustainable livelihood opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
